{"max_tokens":4096,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":"{"claim":"The NutriNet-Sante mortality analysis establishes that reducing ultraprocessed food intake would lower mortality in otherwise unchanged participants.","id":"q-a4722100223cc7c9","packet":{"evidence":"A prospective observational NutriNet-Sante analysis included 44,551 French adults aged at least 45 who supplied at least three 24-hour dietary records. Ultra-processed food intake was expressed as a proportion of total food weight. During median follow-up 7.1 years, 602 deaths occurred. After adjustment for measured demographic, lifestyle and diet factors, each ten-percentage-point higher proportion was associated with mortality hazard ratio 1.14 (95% CI 1.04 to 1.27).","source":{"doi":"10.1001/jamainternmed.2018.7289","title":"Association Between Ultraprocessed Food Consumption and Risk of Mortality Among Middle-aged Adults in France.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/30742202/","version":"Indexed primary abstract body sha256:bc87d6f86c117711ce4d02b50abd687f7956b125855771f1c2df8204236839f0; publication 2019-04-01"}}}"}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","system":"Classify the claim using only the supplied evidence packet and the common label definitions. Select one permitted label. Report confidence as a number from 0 to 1 representing the probability that your selected label is correct, and provide the concise explanation required by the common output schema. Return only the required JSON object.

