{"max_tokens":4096,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":"{"claim":"In RECOVERY, dexamethasone reduced 28-day mortality in hospitalized COVID-19 patients receiving respiratory support at randomization; the trial did not demonstrate that benefit in the subgroup receiving no respiratory support.","id":"q-2707244776dcbae5","packet":{"evidence":"In the final RECOVERY report, hospitalized COVID-19 patients were randomized open-label to dexamethasone 6 mg daily for up to 10 days (2,104 patients) or usual care (4,321). Overall 28-day mortality was 22.9% versus 25.7%, age-adjusted rate ratio 0.83 (95% CI 0.75 to 0.93). At randomization, invasively ventilated patients had mortality 29.3% versus 41.4%, rate ratio 0.64 (0.51 to 0.81); patients on oxygen without invasive ventilation had 23.3% versus 26.2%, rate ratio 0.82 (0.72 to 0.94); patients receiving no respiratory support had 17.8% versus 14.0%, rate ratio 1.19 (0.92 to 1.55).","source":{"doi":"10.1056/nejmoa2021436","title":"Dexamethasone in Hospitalized Patients with Covid-19.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32678530/","version":"Indexed primary abstract body sha256:477b16531e8b21367d13fe77e0679ff918810b146519942096c2020ea87f9f7d; publication 2020-07-17; final RECOVERY NEJM 2021;384:693-704, PMID 32678530"}}}"}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","system":"Classify the claim using only the supplied evidence packet and the common label definitions. Select one permitted label. Report confidence as a number from 0 to 1 representing the probability that your selected label is correct, and provide the concise explanation required by the common output schema. Return only the required JSON object.

