{"max_tokens":4096,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":"{"claim":"These experiments establish longer survival for solid-tumor patients by using anti-CD47 antibodies to remove the signal that protects tumor cells from macrophages.","id":"q-7f0ca6e5ec639574","packet":{"evidence":"CD47 binds SIRP-alpha on phagocytic cells and provides a signal that inhibits engulfment. Experiments with human tumor cells showed that anti-CD47 antibodies enabled macrophage phagocytosis in vitro. In immunodeficient mice carrying patient-derived tumor xenografts, antibody administration inhibited tumor growth and increased mouse survival; an immunocompetent mouse breast-tumor model was also studied. Human patient tumor tissue was used for expression measurements and to establish xenografts; the report describes antibody treatment outcomes in mice.","source":{"doi":"10.1073/pnas.1121623109","title":"The CD47-signal regulatory protein alpha (SIRPa) interaction is a therapeutic target for human solid tumors.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/22451913/","version":"Indexed primary abstract body sha256:b9441c2f13a6df5ecb7b3dd34e0bea7dab6321ab9cd477e79d9a2e2b4d5e30bb; publication 2012-03-26"}}}"}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","system":"Classify the claim using only the supplied evidence packet and the common label definitions. Select one permitted label. Report confidence as a number from 0 to 1 representing the probability that your selected label is correct, and provide the concise explanation required by the common output schema. Return only the required JSON object.

